<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador reserves $1.47 billion at Aug 16.</title>
<headline>Ecuador reserves $1.47 billion at Aug 16.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Monday its net international reserves at August 16 stood at $1.472 billion, unchanged from the previous week.</p>
<p>In the week to August 9, foreign currency reserves fell $133 million.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $1.556 billion.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom 5932 258-433</p>
